2. `Frame::destroy` exact rewrite. Need to be careful about order and invariants. Current:

```cpp
void
Frame::destroy(void)
{
	FORLIST(lnk, this->objectList)
		ObjectWithFrame::fromFrame(lnk)->setFrame(nil);
	s_plglist.destruct(this);
	if(this->getParent())
		this->removeChild();
	if(this->object.privateFlags & Frame::HIERARCHYSYNC)
		this->inDirtyList.remove();
	for(Frame *f = this->child; f; f = f->next)
		f->object.parent = nil;
	rwFree(this);
	numAllocated--;
}
```

Proposed:

```cpp
void
Frame::destroy(void)
{
	FORLIST(lnk, this->objectList)
		ObjectWithFrame::fromFrame(lnk)->setFrame(nil);
	s_plglist.destruct(this);
	Frame *child = this->child;
	this->child = nil;
	for(Frame *c = child; c; c = c->next){
		c->object.parent = nil;
		c->setHierarchyRoot(c);
		c->updateObjects();
	}
	if(this->getParent())
		this->removeChild();
	if(this->object.privateFlags & Frame::HIERARCHYSYNC)
		this->inDirtyList.remove();
	rwFree(this);
	numAllocated--;
}
```

Wait: `removeChild()` is called after setting `this->child=nil`, so it won't re-root them. But `removeChild` does `parent->child` manipulation: it searches `parent->child` chain; if the frame is not found, it could crash (while(child->next != this) child = child->next; if not found → null deref). It's still in the parent's child list, so fine. `removeChild` calls `setHierarchyRoot(this)` (no children) and `updateObjects()` (adds this to dirty list, flag set), then the next `if` removes it from the list. Good.

But order: should we re-root children before `s_plglist.destruct(this)`? Plugins destruct of the frame might include visibility plugin only; child plugin unrelated. Fine.

One subtlety: `c->updateObjects()` may access `engine->frameDirtyList`; valid. It also adds `c` to the dirty list and sets HIERARCHYSYNC on c. Good. But when the parent frame is later freed, c is independent.

However, note `this->object.privateFlags` might still be set with HIERARCHYSYNC from before (if `this` was a root). If `removeChild` is skipped (no parent), the `if` removes it. Fine.

